{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529650-homebrew-the-ten-paths","id":1529650,"title":"Homebrew - The Ten Paths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-29T09:39:58-08:00","id":1529650,"title":"Homebrew - The Ten Paths","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I wanted to have some feedback on a project of mine. I find the idea to put Arcana in pairs to be a bit restrictive. If I have a Moros and I want to go full creator of imbued item, I find myself with an affinity for an Arcana I will not use (Death), and that a waste.<br /> <br /> So I had the idea to rework the Paths system. Now Mages awaken at one of the ten Paths, each with its own Watchtower and Supernal Realm.<br /> <br /> <u>Ruling Arcana:</u> The one from their Paths and one chosen freely.<br /> <br /> <u>Inferior Arcanum:</u> One chosen freely.<br /> <br /> Here the different Paths and their associated Realm, Arcana, Watchtower and Supernal Entities. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Arcana</b></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Path</b></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Realm</b></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Watchtower</b></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Entities</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Death</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Moros</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Stygia</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Leaden Coin</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Shades</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Fate</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Acanthus</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Arcadia</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Silver Mists</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Fae</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Forces</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Aradris</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Malakut</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Bright Flame</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Djinn</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Life</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Thyrsus</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Primal Wild</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Evergrowing Tree</span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Beasts</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Matter</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Naotos</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Hidden Caverns</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Thousand Gems</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Apeirons</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Mind</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Mastigos</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Pandemonium</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Cruel Gauntlet</span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Demons</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Prime</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Obrimos</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Aether</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Golden Key</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Angels</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Space</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Loros</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Endless Web</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Iron Chains</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Imps</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Spirits</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Ibus</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Singing Stones</span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Stone Book</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Totem</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Time</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Cruros</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><i>Chronos</i></span></td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Lunargent Thorns</td> <td width=\"20%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Anachronism</td> </tr> </table></div> My addition are in red.<br /> <br /> I am working on Paths tools and possibly a version of the Vision of Truth chapter from Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? I am open to new idea on the names (especially Realm and Path names, I satisfied with the Watchtowers Name I came up with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26068-apregis","name":"Apregis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26068_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T15:19:22-08:00","id":1529668,"title":"","content":"10 Choose 3 makes 120 possible combinations, Choose 2 (with a set inferior) would reduce it to 45 distinct paths.<br /> <br /> I don't think an item makers with an Affinity for Death is actually a bad thing. Geist has rules for mementos, and Spirit rules for Craft Fetish, so binding a ghost to an item to access their power seems like an entirely appropriate use of Death for your average Moros, plus adding a ruling path via joining a Legacy.<br /> <br /> I prefer to reduce to 5 Arcana, each with a gross and subtle aspect, but that works better in a pre-fall high fantasy setting.<br /> <br /> Why does each Mage walk two paths? And do they sign on to two watchtowers? I think the infinity of Supernal Realms with 45 combinations which mages have identified makes sense. Space-Time as a realm is rather Einsteinian, for example. Would love to see Emanation realms along the lines of mixed Arcana...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T16:56:39-08:00","id":1529673,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, have you taken a look at the <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/82216/Mage-Chroniclers-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Chronicler's Guide</a>? It's First Edition, but the material on pages 95-103 discusses alternative approaches to the Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T17:46:41-08:00","id":1529674,"title":"","content":"Death is not necessarily a bad Arcana for crafting, especially when paired with the Prime 4 needed for imbued items. With Death 1 and Prime 1, you can make an imbued item that reveals the full truth behind a lie, because you Know how that lie ends/dies.<br /> <br /> Death 2 and Prime 2 allows you to make an item that can decay spells, eroding at their Potency, giving more Reach to play around with.<br /> <br /> With Death 3 and Prime 5 / Matter 4 you can use a variation of Eidolon to animate the user's shadow, making them into a bodyguard, assistant or spy (since they are naturally invisible when there is no light).<br /> <br /> Utilizing Death 4 and Prime 4, you can make an item that devours the cold rather than the wounded. Now you can consume levels of cold environmental tilts for mana, rejoicing as your Sanctum's heating system empowers your spells.<br /> <br /> Lastly with Death 5 and Prime 1 you can create a phurba, which can be used to immobilize any Throne aligned Supernal entity or a being with a soul touched by the Exarchs (such as a Prelate).<br /> <br /> Hopefully those examples showcase some of the cool utility that Death brings to imbuing.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Paths, I think the Djinn might be a better fit for Spirit, since they are known to wield a plethora of abilities, sometimes needed to be exorcised and were famously bound by king Solomon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T18:00:49-08:00","id":1529676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529650-homebrew-the-ten-paths?p=1529674#post1529674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death is not necessarily a bad Arcana for crafting, especially when paired with the Prime 4 needed for imbued items. With Death 1 and Prime 1, you can make an imbued item that reveals the full truth behind a lie, because you Know how that lie ends/dies.<br /> <br /> Death 2 and Prime 2 allows you to make an item that can decay spells, eroding at their Potency, giving more Reach to play around with.<br /> <br /> With Death 3 and Prime 5 / Matter 4 you can use a variation of Eidolon to animate the user's shadow, making them into a bodyguard, assistant or spy (since they are naturally invisible when there is no light).<br /> <br /> Utilizing Death 4 and Prime 4, you can make an item that devours the cold rather than the wounded. Now you can consume levels of cold environmental tilts for mana, rejoicing as your Sanctum's heating system empowers your spells.<br /> <br /> Lastly with Death 5 and Prime 1 you can create a phurba, which can be used to immobilize any Throne aligned Supernal entity or a being with a soul touched by the Exarchs (such as a Prelate).<br /> <br /> Hopefully those examples showcase some of the cool utility that Death brings to imbuing.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Paths, I think the Djinn might be a better fit for Spirit, since they are known to wield a plethora of abilities, sometimes needed to be exorcised and were famously bound by king Solomon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells really that flexible? The first example seems like a huge stretch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T18:58:05-08:00","id":1529682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529650-homebrew-the-ten-paths?p=1529676#post1529676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells really that flexible? The first example seems like a huge stretch</div> </div> </div> </div>The first example follows a similar train of thought as the Singers in Silence (found on page 169 of the Mysterium's Order book) for their first Attainment. They utilize Death and Fate in an Unveiling to hear when a subject's immediate future will end in death, at least if it remains unchanged. So applying a similar approach to <i>Pierce Deception</i>, it should be possible to use conjunctional Death to know how a lie ends/dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T06:57:09-08:00","id":1529709,"title":"","content":"I think the Death example spells of crafting shadows, or taking items from twilight and making them solid are good too.<br /> <br /> A pure crafter who uses ghost ephemera/ectoplasm as a resource to manipulate and craft would make a terrifying legacy. Pulling items out of next to nothing (like Platonic Forms, but fueled by plasm rather than Mana).<br /> <br /> Shadow shaping and manipulating the Strix (instead of ghost bodies) sounds like another possible legacy direction... If more dangerous..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"typos) 01-30-2024, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T14:03:32-08:00","id":1529769,"title":"","content":"The Death crafter was only an exemple. I merely find the fact than you can have an affinity for an Arcana you don't want to use. If you want to be an Alchemist but not a Necromancer for exemple, or a scientist mage with Forces/Matter and don't want to use either Prime or Death. With the curent system only the Legacies can help you and you still have a unused affinity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529650-homebrew-the-ten-paths?p=1529673#post1529673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, have you taken a look at the <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/82216/Mage-Chroniclers-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Chronicler's Guide</a>? It's First Edition, but the material on pages 95-103 discusses alternative approaches to the Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any 1e books so I couldn't read the Chronicle's Guide, but I read somewhere on the Sixth Watchtowers, that gave me the idea for the Force Tower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529650-homebrew-the-ten-paths?p=1529668#post1529668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10 Choose 3 makes 120 possible combinations, Choose 2 (with a set inferior) would reduce it to 45 distinct paths.<br /> <br /> I don't think an item makers with an Affinity for Death is actually a bad thing. Geist has rules for mementos, and Spirit rules for Craft Fetish, so binding a ghost to an item to access their power seems like an entirely appropriate use of Death for your average Moros, plus adding a ruling path via joining a Legacy.<br /> <br /> I prefer to reduce to 5 Arcana, each with a gross and subtle aspect, but that works better in a pre-fall high fantasy setting.<br /> <br /> Why does each Mage walk two paths? And do they sign on to two watchtowers? I think the infinity of Supernal Realms with 45 combinations which mages have identified makes sense. Space-Time as a realm is rather Einsteinian, for example. Would love to see Emanation realms along the lines of mixed Arcana...</div> </div> </div> </div>You got as primary arcana the arcana of your Path, the you choose a secondary arcana freely who work like the primary (like Supernal being, they have a primary linked to their Realm and a second, coming from any Realm). And you got to choose your Inferior Arcanum.<br /> <br /> At first I was thinking having a Realms for each pairs, but that too much to kept track and find names. But as I did you can choose any pair of primary arcana and inferior arcanum with a minium amount of Realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26068-apregis","name":"Apregis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26068_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}